Fix round 3 is done: the suite passes **138/138** (was 82/82) with zero console errors, zero warnings and every request `file://`. It took two runs to get there, and the first-run crash is not fully explained.

## What changed

- **Popup overlap (A):** floating labels are laid out every frame. The newest sits beside the event and any older label that would touch it is lifted clear above; labels are clamped to the road width. Fare and combo remain two labels, both with a heavier dark outline.
- **HORN READY:** it no longer uses the float path. `HORN READY!` and `HORN CHARGING` are drawn as a tag in the right road-side gutter at about 42% of screen height, wrapping to two lines on narrow phones. It is never on the tarmac or near the matatu.
- **Rooftops (1):** height tiers with cast shadows, split plots, parapet ledges or corrugated roofs, stair bulkheads, water tanks on stands with a feed pipe, and AC units. All Canvas, no image files.
- **Headlight (2):** two soft radial lobes that fade out at about 3 lanes. It now reads fairly faint.
- **Popup outline (3):** the outline is now 26% of text size, near-black.
- **Text and phone layout (4):**
  - Every visible text is at least 14px.
  - The demo line is now "DEMO. Esc for menu".
  - In portrait the road takes about 53% of the width, leaving a 36px shop strip each side at 390x844 and 29px at 320x568.
  - Pause and mute stack in the right gutter on narrow screens.
- **How to play (5):** the title has a five-tile icon row, and the full cards and controls live in a "How to play" sheet. Nothing clips or scrolls at 320x568, 844x390, 390x844 or 1280x720; the Start row also stays on screen at 360x640.
- **Kanjo icon (6):** a dedicated high-contrast icon (fat striped boom, glowing beacons, lime vest, white cap), plus a modest in-world contrast pass. Hitboxes are unchanged.
- **Fonts (7):** Barlow Condensed Black Italic for display and canvas text, Rajdhani for body, wired with relative `@font-face` urls. Impact is removed, the static scan allows only those local font urls, and the README documents the OFL fonts.

## Evidence

- **Popups:** no two popup rectangles overlapped in 329 sampled frames of the seed 7 demo or 413 frames of the keyboard run. Combo and fare were visible together in 208 demo frames, and HORN READY together with pickup text in 32. See `out/screenshots/12-popups-fare-combo-hornready-desktop.png`.
- **Audio:**
  - No AudioContext exists before a gesture.
  - After Start the context is `running` with music on and peak RMS about 0.43; it goes silent when muted and is audible again when unmuted.
  - Sound-effect counts match the event log (14 pickup sounds for 14 pickups, 1 horn).
- **Recording:** `out/gameplay-demo.mp4` (21.9s) is the seed 7 demo started by a real click, with the game's own audio muxed in (mean -11.8 dB). `out/gameplay.mp4` is the 20s cut with audio kept; sound starts about 1s in, at the click.
- **Screenshots:** title, how-to, play and pause at all four sizes are in `out/screenshots/` and on the contact sheet.

## Caveats

- **First test run crashed.** The seed 42 autostart demo did not reach its tick target in 40s. I could not reproduce it standalone, so I added Chrome anti-throttling flags and `bringToFront`, and the second run passed. That run also showed 8 false failures from my own clip detector, which I fixed.
- **A commit I did not make.** `c500630 WIP round 3: Claude edits` (author "Fundi") appeared mid-session and contains most of this work. I made no commits.
- **Third fix round.** `EVAL.md` allows two; I left the self-score at 36/40 and noted this in `SELF-EVAL.md`.
- **Unreviewed visuals and sound.** The art, typography and headlight were judged by me from screenshots; nobody has listened to the audio.
- **320px combo chip.** On 320px-wide screens the combo chip covers most of the left shop strip while a combo is live.
- **Sampling rate.** Popup overlap is sampled every 20–25ms, not on every rendered frame.

